cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "An LLM Auditor for Hospital Readmission Alerts: Independent Verification Beyond Prediction"
abstract: >
  A three-stage readmission prediction pipeline: a capacity-constrained XGBoost
  screen on structured EHR features (Stage 1), an independent Clinical-Longformer
  risk estimate from discharge notes (Stage 2), and a local MedGemma-27B model
  (Stage 3) that independently audits each of Stage 1's flagged cases —
  reasoning over both scores, the percentile-rank displacement between them,
  and the note itself — to extract quoted, individually-verified mitigating
  and aggravating grounds, reach its own uphold/override/insufficient-
  evidence decision, and report a second decision recomputed deterministically
  from those grounds as a transparency check. Trained and evaluated on
  MIMIC-IV; at matched alert volume the structured screen alone outperforms
  the full three-stage cascade, a validated negative result.
